[WORK]
UID: WORK-SDOC-CONTEXT-LOADING
TITLE: Loading agent context from the canon
DEPTH: sketch
AUTHORED_BY: llm
STATEMENT: >>>
Loading agent context out of the canon, rather than authoring it twice. Two
routes are on the table and neither is chosen: projecting selected sdoc nodes
into the existing per-ecosystem instruction files (steering, rules,
instructions), or a hook that injects nodes into a session at start or at a
checkpoint. The open questions are which nodes qualify, how they are selected,
and whether the projection is generated at build time or read live. Undecided.
<<<
NOTES: >>>
The operator, verbatim: "and another sdoc for loading context from sdocs (e.g.,
sdoc -> steering or some other system like hooks could be on the table)."
<<<
